    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on favorable matchups today, anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Gunnar Henderson** (73.30), our top-scoring options. **Jackson Merrill** faces Michael McGreevy, benefiting from a +13% platoon edge and a high-volume batting order slot, while **Gunnar Henderson** maintains a robust score despite facing a left-hander; his performance is buoyed significantly by a +16% park factor and the expectation that he provides elite production regardless of handedness. **Coby Mayo** (63.97) and **Sam Antonacci** (60.82) also grade out as strong starts, with **Sam Antonacci** bolstered by his elite xwOBA (0.398) and a prime leadoff spot against Emerson Hancock, positioning him as a high-upside play for run production.\n\nThe optimization process was tight regarding the bench, with **Miguel Vargas** (51.54) just missing the cut. While **Miguel Vargas** offers solid value against Emerson Hancock, he was edged out by **Marcell Ozuna** (51.56) and **Heliot Ramos** (51.63), as the model prioritized the latter\u2019s lineup stability and the slight weather advantage\u2014specifically the wind blowing out\u2014for **Heliot Ramos**. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Josh Lowe** (49.81); while facing the formidable Dylan Cease is a risk, **Josh Lowe** retains value due to the slow delivery of the opposing pitcher, which creates an opportunity to steal a base\u2014a priority given our scarcity strategy.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding the top of our order, as the lineup for **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** remains pending. Both catchers face pitchers with xERAs in the 3.00\u20134.30 range, and any shift in batting order could further compress their efficiency scores. Furthermore, **Kyle Tucker** (52.24) faces an elite arm in Chris Sale; while his pedigree demands a start, the -19% SP skill penalty necessitates a tempered expectation for his output today. All roster decisions remain subject to real-time adjustments once final lineups are confirmed.",
